/* ===================== *
 *     Voidstalker       *
 * ===================== */
@901 = ~voidstalker~
@902 = ~Voidstalker~
@903 = ~Voidstalker:

A supernatural assassin who combines conventional thievery with powers drawn from the void. Voidstalkers channel this energy into their ambushes, striking through magical defenses that stop ordinary assassination techniques.

Advantages:
- 1st level: Gains the Unbound Instinct passive ability.

Unbound Instinct:
The Voidstalker's exposure to the void sharpens <PRO_HISHER> reflexes and allows <PRO_HIMHER> to anticipate attacks before they happen.
<PRO_HISHER> movements become difficult to follow, while <PRI_HISHER> strikes find weaknesses in even the most heavily defended opponents.
The Voidstalker gains a permanent +1 bonus to THAC0 and AC.

- 1st level: Gains the Netherstrike passive ability.

Netherstrike:
Rather than striking at their victim's body, Voidstalkers tear open a fleeting rift into the emptiness between planes, allowing tendrils of void energy to surge through their weapon and into the target.
These supernatural ambushes rend the victim's very essence, inflicting magical damage that cannot be stopped by ordinary physical defenses.

Instead of a traditional backstab multiplier, attacks made while invisible deal additional magical damage, regardless of the target's backstab immunity or the attacker's position.
1st level: +2d6
5th level: +4d6
10th level: +6d6
15th level: +8d6
20th level: +10d6

This damage bypasses weapon protection spells such as Protection From Magical Weapons (requires EEex).

- 5st level: May use the Shadow Step ability once per day, gaining an additional use every 4 levels thereafter.

Shadow Step:
The Voidstalker slips through the void, teleporting a short distance and becoming invisible for 1 round.

- 8th level: May use the Void Prision ability once per day, gaining an additional use every 6 levels thereafter.

Void Prison:
The Voidstalker tears open a dimensional rift around an enemy, enclosing it within a sphere of condensed void energy.
For 1 turn, the target is enclosed in an invulnerable globe of shimmering force if they fail a saving throw vs. spells at a -2 penalty.
Hence, the creature caught inside the globe is completely safe from all attacks, but at the same time completely unable to affect the outside world.

- 10th level: Unbound Instinct Bonus increases to +2 THAC0 and AC.
- 20th level: Unbound Instinct Bonus increases to +3 THAC0 and AC.

- High-Level Ability: Void Execution replaces Assassination.

Disadvantages:
- No normal backstab multiplier.
- Cannot set traps: the Set Spike Trap, Set Explosive Trap and Set Time Trap high-level abilities are not available.~

